Holli Dance is David White's 3D dancer for SGI workstations: Holli dances
in a night club, with club lighting, to the music on the audio input
(Digital In by default; without audio she dances anyway). Its frame rate,
shown under Rendering, is a well-known SGI graphics benchmark. The 1998
version, which the sgidepot.co.uk benchmark table uses, is in
hollidance-classic; the author notes that 1.6's frame rates do not compare
with it.

This is the author's IRIX binary (n32, OpenGL, Motif, audio). Run it with
"hollidance", which keeps your settings in ~/.hollidance; with the
hollidance-models package, "hollidance -large" uses the large models.

The NoStrobe file keeps the strobe light effect off, because strobing
light can cause seizures in people with epilepsy. The hollidance command
always keeps it in place.
